### project-portfolio-management-service — example requests
# project-portfolio-management/project-portfolio-management-service-with-loco
# — loco-idiomatic layout (src/controllers/). Envelope: BARE loco JSON,
# same posture as organization.http — see that file's header. Gated by
# PROJECT_PORTFOLIO_MANAGEMENT_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off). One recursive
# `Plan` type — `kind` (Project/Portfolio/Product/Program/...) is an
# optional descriptive label, never a matching or routing gate.
#
# This crate has the widest surface in the family (Kanban, sprints,
# burndown, goals, governance, strategy, risk, …) — see AGENTS.md for
# the complete module list. This file covers plan CRUD + match/dedupe
# plus the flagship engineering sub-resources (tasks, sprints, burndown).
#
# GOTCHA: unlike the other loco-idiomatic crates, plan create has NO
# 409-on-duplicate path (curl-verified against the code, not just
# behaviour) — creating the same name twice does not conflict.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8090
@planPid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_CREATE
# curl-verified example: creating the body below in a local run produced
# pid 6cc2d9aa-8e85-47cc-ae6b-5619c73c6aab — copy your own create
# response's "pid" instead of reusing this one.
@sprintPid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_SPRINT_CREATE
@taskPid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_TASK_CREATE
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/_health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a plan — minimal valid body. `kind` is descriptive only.
# curl-verified response: {"pid":"<uuid>","name":"Apollo platform migration"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "kind": "Project",
  "name": "Apollo platform migration",
  "code": "PROJ-2026",
  "owner_org_id": "organization:9a2f",
  "goals": [{ "title": "Cut p95 latency" }],
  "keywords": ["infra"],
  "identifiers": [{ "scheme": "JiraProjectKey", "value": "APOLLO" }]
}


### Get the created plan back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}


### List — paginated (curl-verified X-Total-Count/X-Limit/X-Offset headers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans?limit=25&offset=0


### Search — fuzzy + phonetic via Tantivy; `kind` is a filter, never a
# matching gate.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/search?q=Apollo&fuzzy=true&kind=Project


### Probabilistic + deterministic match — kind-agnostic (any two plans
# may match regardless of their `kind` label)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/match
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Apollo platform migration", "owner_org_id": "organization:9a2f" }


### Explicit duplicate check — curl-verified: bare `[]` when no candidates
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Apollo platform migration" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate plans (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_pid": "{{planPid}}", "duplicate_pid": "<other-uuid>" }


### Kanban — create a task under this plan
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Set up CI" }


### Kanban — list this plan's tasks (curl-verified: grouped with a
# `counts` summary by status alongside the flat `tasks` array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/tasks


### Kanban — move a task (PATCH; WIP-limit capped per column)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/tasks/{{taskPid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }


### Create a sprint — `starts_on`/`ends_on` are REQUIRED (curl-verified:
# `{"name":...}` alone 422s).
# @name createSprint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/sprints
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sprint 1", "starts_on": "2026-01-01", "ends_on": "2026-01-14" }


### Burndown for a sprint — `sprint` query param is REQUIRED
# (curl-verified: omitting it 400s "missing field `sprint`"). There is
# no separate /timeline endpoint — burndown is the shipped operational
# view (agents/share/overview.md capability matrix).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/burndown?sprint={{sprintPid}}


### Velocity across this plan's sprints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/velocity


### Masked view (privacy.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}/audit


### Delete (soft-delete) a plan
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planPid}}
